# Where the model (mbf.py, the 1983 source's arithmetic) and PC-BASIC 2.0.7 differ on math.bas, and why
# (check.py's oracle check). The project's own. Each line: the expression, then why. A difference not listed
# fails, and so does a line listed whose difference has gone. Where the reason is PC-BASIC's own function,
# PC-BASIC computes the function in IEEE double precision and converts it, a unit lower in the last digit
# more often than not; it doesn't run GW-BASIC's Hart polynomials, so it can't settle those bits. The
# arithmetic itself (+ - * / in each precision, $FIN, $FOUT, INT, FIX, CSNG, CDBL, RND's generator) agrees
# everywhere it is printed.
SQR(2)                     # GW-BASIC's root a bit at a time rounds its 25th bit; PC-BASIC's is a unit lower
SQR(.5)                    # GW-BASIC's root a bit at a time rounds its 25th bit; PC-BASIC's is a unit lower
SQR(10)                    # GW-BASIC's root a bit at a time rounds its 25th bit; PC-BASIC's is a unit lower
SQR(123456.7)              # GW-BASIC's root a bit at a time rounds its 25th bit; PC-BASIC's is a unit lower
SQR(9.999999E-39)          # GW-BASIC's root a bit at a time rounds its 25th bit; PC-BASIC's is a unit lower
EXP(-1)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(50)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(-50)                   # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(87)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(88)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(-88)                   # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(3.5)                   # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
EXP(20.25)                 # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
LOG(.5)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
LOG(1.000001)              # cancellation: LOG is P/Q of the mantissa plus the exponent, -1+1 here; PC-BASIC is accurate
LOG(.999999)               # cancellation: LOG is P/Q of the mantissa plus the exponent, -1+1 here; PC-BASIC is accurate
SIN(2)                     # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(3.141593)              # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(1.570796)              # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(4.712389)              # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(10)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(100)                   # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(1000)                  # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
SIN(1E-4)                  # GW-BASIC returns a tiny x as SIN(x) (and ATN, TAN near it); PC-BASIC 9.999999E-0n
SIN(1E-6)                  # GW-BASIC returns a tiny x as SIN(x) (and ATN, TAN near it); PC-BASIC 9.999999E-0n
COS(2)                     # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
COS(3)                     # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
COS(3.141593)              # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
COS(6.283185)              # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
COS(10)                    # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
COS(100)                   # PC-BASIC's own function, a unit off in the last digit: not the 1983 Hart polynomial
